{
  "id": "Compound::DB01035 - Gene::6336",
  "verbalization": "Procainamide exhibits a strong binding relationship with Scn7a and Scn8a, both of which are involved in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, and this activity is linked to Scn10a. The evidence suggests that Procainamide may modulate Scn10a through its interaction with sodium channels, potentially influencing neuronal excitability. The similarity between Procainamide and Oxybuprocaine, and between Oxybuprocaine and Proparacaine, further supports a shared mechanism of action, with Proparacaine directly binding to Scn10a. This implies that Procainamide may exert its effects on Scn10a via a similar pathway, possibly through interactions with sodium channels. The integrated evidence suggests a plausible mechanistic link between Procainamide and Scn10a, mediated by sodium channel activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
